COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[290,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nMaintain all daily prayers in the Mosque, especially Al-Fajr.\nPray tonight as much as you can, then conclude with Witr prayer.\nPerform Ruqyah (supplication for healing) on yourself or on those around you.\nguid\nThe Quran is a source of healing and mercy for the believers, so seek healing from it for your physical and spiritual maladies.\nWhen the people of truth spread it out, falsehood will definitely diminish even if it became inflated for a while.\nBeware of wrongdoing, as a wrongdoer is deprived from benefiting from the Quran commensurate with the extent of his wrongdoing.\nrefl\nوَإِن كَادُواْ لَيَسۡتَفِزُّونَكَ مِنَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ لِيُخۡرِجُوكَ مِنۡهَاۖ وَإِذٗا لَّا يَلۡبَثُونَ خِلَٰفَكَ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ٧٦\nMeaning: Had they driven you out of Makkah, they would not have remained after you except for a short time. When the Prophet (ﷺ) migrated from Makkah to Al-Madinah due to Quraish harassment of him and his Companions, the polytheists did not remain after that except for a little while, and most of them ended up killed in the battle of Badr. Ibn Juzay: 1/494.\nExplain the way of Allah in dealing with those who harm preachers and reformers.\nوَمِنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ فَتَهَجَّدۡ بِهِۦ نَافِلَةٗ لَّكَ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَبۡعَثَكَ رَبُّكَ مَقَامٗا مَّحۡمُودٗا ٧٩\nAs narrated in Sahih Al-Bukhari, Abdullah bin Omar (t) said: On the Day of Resurrection, people will become groups where each nation will follow its Prophet, saying: \"O so and so, intercede for us,\" until the intercession ends with Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ), and that is the Day when Allah will raise him to the praised status. Ibn Ashur: 15/185.\nWhat is meant by (the praised status)?\nوَمِنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ فَتَهَجَّدۡ بِهِۦ نَافِلَةٗ لَّكَ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَبۡعَثَكَ رَبُّكَ مَقَامٗا مَّحۡمُودٗا ٧٩\nNighttime prayer has solitude and communing with Allah (the Creator) away from people. Al-Qurtubi: 13/151.\nNighttime prayer has a distinctive quality that is not found in other acts of worship. What is it?\nوَقُلۡ جَآءَ ٱلۡحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ ٱلۡبَٰطِلُۚ إِنَّ ٱلۡبَٰطِلَ كَانَ زَهُوقٗا ٨١\nThis is the nature of falsehood, but it may have the upper hand for a while if it is not opposed by the truth. But when the truth comes, falsehood diminishes and ends up lifeless. Hence, falsehood is only popular at times and in places where there is no knowledge of the revelations and proofs of Allah. Al-Saadi: 465.\nWhen does falsehood become strong and have the upper hand?\nوَقُلۡ جَآءَ ٱلۡحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ ٱلۡبَٰطِلُۚ إِنَّ ٱلۡبَٰطِلَ كَانَ زَهُوقٗا ٨١\n(Indeed, falsehood is bound to perish) this indicates that perishing is a constant habit of falsehood, where every time it appears, it soon becomes perished. Ibn Ashur: 15/188.\nWhat is the indication of this verse: (indeed, falsehood is bound to perish)?\nوَنُنَزِّلُ مِنَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ مَا هُوَ شِفَآءٞ وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ\nThe healing that is contained in the Quran is broad in scope, and offers healing for spiritual maladies such as doubt, ignorance, corrupt views, deviation and bad intentions. It also contains certain knowledge by means of which all doubts may be dispelled, and exhortation and reminders that dispel all desires that are contrary to the command of Allah. It also offers healing from physical pain and sickness. Al-Saadi: 465.\nHow does the Quran heal the hearts?\nوَيَسۡـَٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلرُّوحِۖ قُلِ ٱلرُّوحُ مِنۡ أَمۡرِ رَبِّي وَمَآ أُوتِيتُم مِّنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ٨٥\nThis verse indicates that if a person is asked about something when it would have been more appropriate to ask about something else, he should refrain from answering and point the questioner toward what he needs to know and which will benefit him. Al-Saadi: 466.\nPeople often ask about useless things. How should the preacher deal with that?\nwords\nكَادُواThey were about\nتَحوِيلًاAn alteration\nلِدُلُوكِ الشَّمسِThe decline of the sun\nغَسَقِ اللَّيلِDarkness of the night\nوَزَهَقَHas perished\nزَهُوقًاBound to perish\nوَنَأَى بِجَانِبِهِHe turns away from the obedience of Allah and becomes arrogant\nشَاكِلَتِهِHis manner"],[291,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nIdentify five of Allah's biggest favors upon you, then thank Him for them.\nRead an example from the Quran, and draw a lesson from it.\nLook for a good translation of the meanings of the Quran and give it to a disbeliever so that he may accept Islam.\nguid\nAllah has diversified admonitions and examples in the Quran so that their intended meanings are realized.\nLearn the skills of dialogue and debate, and rehearse them.\nWhenever you face difficulties, read the Prophetic biography so that you follow the example of the Prophet (ﷺ) on how to be patient.\nrefl\nإِلَّا رَحۡمَةٗ مِّن رَّبِّكَۚ إِنَّ فَضۡلَهُۥ كَانَ عَلَيۡكَ كَبِيرٗا ٨٧\nMeaning: Allah made you the leader of the children of Adam, and gave you the praised status and this Holy book. Al-Qurtubi: 13/151.\nWhat are the great favors bestowed by Allah upon His Prophet (ﷺ)?\nقُل لَّئِنِ ٱجۡتَمَعَتِ ٱلۡإِنسُ وَٱلۡجِنُّ عَلَىٰٓ أَن يَأۡتُواْ بِمِثۡلِ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ لَا يَأۡتُونَ بِمِثۡلِهِۦ وَلَوۡ كَانَ بَعۡضُهُمۡ لِبَعۡضٖ ظَهِيرٗا ٨٨\nCreated beings are unable to produce something similar to the Quran because of what it contains of divine knowledge, clear proofs, nonpareil meanings of which most people were not aware nor could they reach, and all that came with perfection. Most people said that they were unable to match the Quran because of its eloquence, perfect style, and many other aspects of its inimitability. Ibn Juzay: 1/496.\nExplain some of the inimitable aspects of the Holy Quran.\nقُل لَّئِنِ ٱجۡتَمَعَتِ ٱلۡإِنسُ وَٱلۡجِنُّ عَلَىٰٓ أَن يَأۡتُواْ بِمِثۡلِ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ لَا يَأۡتُونَ بِمِثۡلِهِۦ وَلَوۡ كَانَ بَعۡضُهُمۡ لِبَعۡضٖ ظَهِيرٗا ٨٨\nThis is a definitive proof of the soundness and truth of what the Messenger (ﷺ) brought, as Allah challenged humankind and the jinn to produce its like. Moreover, He stated that they would never be able to produce its like; even if they all cooperated to that effect, they would never be able to do it. Thus, it came to pass as Allah told us. Al-Saadi: 466.\nHow does this verse indicate the truthfulness of the Muhammad’s (ﷺ) message?\nقُل لَّئِنِ ٱجۡتَمَعَتِ ٱلۡإِنسُ وَٱلۡجِنُّ عَلَىٰٓ أَن يَأۡتُواْ بِمِثۡلِ هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ لَا يَأۡتُونَ بِمِثۡلِهِۦ وَلَوۡ كَانَ بَعۡضُهُمۡ لِبَعۡضٖ ظَهِيرٗا ٨٨\nThe Quran is inimitable in its style, formation, and information about the unseen. It sits at the highest level of eloquence, and is not similar to the words of created beings because the Quran is an increate; if it was, they would have produce something similar to it. Al-Baghawi: 2/714.\nDescribe some of the inimitable aspects of the Holy Quran.\nوَقَالُواْ لَن نُّؤۡمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّىٰ تَفۡجُرَ لَنَا مِنَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ يَنۢبُوعًا ٩٠\nThis is easy for Allah, may He be glorified and exalted; if He willed, He could do that. He could have responded to all their demands, but He knew that they would not be guided by that. Ibn Kathir: 3/63.\nAllah did not answer the requests of the polytheists. Why?\nأَوۡ تُسۡقِطَ ٱلسَّمَآءَ كَمَا زَعَمۡتَ عَلَيۡنَا كِسَفًا\nMeaning: You promised us that on the Day of Resurrection the heavens will be split asunder, being broken and torn up, with parts of it falling down, so do that in this world and make it fall in pieces. As for the Prophet of Repentance and Mercy who was sent as a mercy to the world, he asked Allah to delay their punishment, in the hope that Allah would bring forth from their offspring people who would worship Allah Alone, with no partner or associate. This is indeed what happened, for among those who are mentioned in this verse were some who later embraced Islam and became good and sincere Muslims. Ibn Kathir: 3/63.\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) did not ask Allah to make the heaven fall in fragments upon those who requested it. Why?\nقُل لَّوۡ كَانَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مَلَٰٓئِكَةٞ يَمۡشُونَ مُطۡمَئِنِّينَ لَنَزَّلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِم مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَلَكٗا رَّسُولٗا ٩٥\n(Say, \"If there were angels walking on earth peacefully\"), angels residing and settled on earth. (We would have certainly sent down to them from the heaven an angel as a messenger) a messenger who is an angel like them because those who are of the same kind are inclined toward each other more than to a different kind. Al-Baghawi: 2/717.\nAllah sent human Prophets, not angels, to the people. Why?\nwords\nظَهِيرًاA collaborator, assistant\nصَرَّفنَاWe diversified, explained\nيَنبُوعًاA spring of flowing water\nكِسَفًاFragments\nقَبِيلًاFace to face\nزُخرُفٍGold"],[292,"§Al-Isra\ndeeds\nPerform ablution perfectly over the extremities of your body so that all of their sins will be forgiven.\nAsk Allah to make you independent of anyone besides Him by His grace.\nGive to charity in order to adapt yourself to generosity.\nguid\nNo matter how generous and giving a person may be, withholding remains his essence, but Allah, the Almighty, is the Most Beneficent, the Munificent who provides without measure.\nThe greater the position of Allah in the servant's heart, the lesser he thinks of anyone else.\nNo matter how much hardship you face, just be patient because the outcome is for the righteous.\nrefl\nوَمَن يَهۡدِ ٱللَّهُ فَهُوَ ٱلۡمُهۡتَدِۖ وَمَن يُضۡلِلۡ فَلَن تَجِدَ لَهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ مِن دُونِهِۦۖ\nMeaning: If Allah guides them, they will be guided. (And whoever He causes to stray, you will find none to protect them besides Him), no one else will guide them. Al-Qurtubi: 13/178.\nCan anyone attain true guidance without the will of Allah?\nوَنَحۡشُرُهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ عَلَىٰ وُجُوهِهِمۡ عُمۡيٗا وَبُكۡمٗا وَصُمّٗاۖ مَّأۡوَىٰهُمۡ جَهَنَّمُۖ\nOn the Day of Resurrection, they will be dragged on their faces to Hellfire, similar to what is done in this life to someone who is put through extreme humiliation and torment. Anas bin Malik narrated: A man said: \"O Allah's Messenger! Those disbelievers who will be gathered on their faces on the Day of Resurrection; how will Allah gather a disbeliever on his face?\" He said, \"Will not the One Who made him walk on his feet in this world be able to make him walk on his face on the Day of Resurrection?\" When Qatadah heard that, he said: \"Yes, by the Power of Our Lord!\" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Al-Qurtubi: 13/178.\nHow will the disbelievers be gathered on their faces on the Day of Resurrection? What is the indication of that?\nوَنَحۡشُرُهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ عَلَىٰ وُجُوهِهِمۡ عُمۡيٗا وَبُكۡمٗا وَصُمّٗاۖ مَّأۡوَىٰهُمۡ جَهَنَّمُۖ كُلَّمَا خَبَتۡ زِدۡنَٰهُمۡ سَعِيرٗا ٩٧\nThis is a befitting recompense for their sins because they promoted falsehood as the truth, and distorted the truth with the markings of falsehood. Thus, they will be punished by having their faces transformed into limbs for walking instead of their feet. Then, they will be (blind and dumb) as a requital for their false claims about the Messenger (ﷺ) and the Quran. They will be (deaf) because turned away from listening to the truth. Ibn Ashur: 15/217.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the disbelievers will be recompensed in accordance to their sins. Explain.\nوَنَحۡشُرُهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ عَلَىٰ وُجُوهِهِمۡ عُمۡيٗا وَبُكۡمٗا وَصُمّٗاۖ مَّأۡوَىٰهُمۡ جَهَنَّمُۖ كُلَّمَا خَبَتۡ زِدۡنَٰهُمۡ سَعِيرٗا ٩٧\nIf it is said: \"How are they described here as blind, dumb and deaf while in another verse Allah says, (The wicked will see the Fire) [18:53], where they can see, speak and hear?\" It is said that they will be gathered as described by Allah, then their senses will be returned to them. In another explanation, (blind and dumb), Ibn Abbas (t) said: \"They will not see what pleases them nor will they be able to present an argument; and (deaf), they will not hear what pleases them.\" Alhasan said: They will be in this situation when they are gathered until they enter Hellfire. Al-Baghawi: 2/718.\nHow will the dwellers of Hellfire be gathered (blind, dumb and deaf)?\nوَكَانَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ قَتُورٗا ١٠٠\nMeaning: Man is stingy and unwilling to spend. Al-Baghawi: 2/719.\nWhat is the inherent characteristic of humans when it comes to dealing with wealth? How can the servant overcome that?\nقَالَ لَقَدۡ عَلِمۡتَ مَآ أَنزَلَ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ إِلَّا رَبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ بَصَآئِرَ وَإِنِّي لَأَظُنُّكَ يَٰفِرۡعَوۡنُ مَثۡبُورٗا ١٠٢\nMoses (u), the truthful, said: (you already know that none sent down these [signs] except the Lord of the heavens and earth as clear proofs), which indicated that Pharaoh was aware that Allah revealed these signs, hence, he was shown to be most stubborn and tyrannical due to his corrupted intentions and purpose, not due to his lack of knowledge. Ibn Taimyah: 4/248.\nA knowledgeable person may go astray. Explain in light of this verse.\nفَأَرَادَ أَن يَسۡتَفِزَّهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَأَغۡرَقۡنَٰهُ وَمَن مَّعَهُۥ جَمِيعٗا ١٠٣\nThe Polytheists intended to drive the Prophet (ﷺ) and Muslims from Makkah, which was similar to what Pharaoh intended of exiling Moses (u) and the Children of Israel from Egypt. Ibn Ashur: 15/228.\nThere is a resemblance between the Polytheists of Quraish and Pharaoh's people. Explain.\nwords\nخَبَتIts flare subsided\nقَتُورًاMiserly\nبَصَائِرَClear proofs of the Oneness of Allah and my truthfulness\nمَثبُورًاDoomed, accursed\nلَفِيفًاAll together"],[293,"§Al-Kahf, Al-Isra\ndeeds\nMemorize the first ten verses from the beginning of Surat Al-Kahf. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Surat Al-Kahf, will be protected from Antichrist (Ad-Dajjal).\" [Sahih Muslim].\nGather with some of your friends, and let each of you recite verses from the Book of Allah (the Quran).\nReflect on the meanings of some of Allah's Names, then invoke Him by them.\nguid\nThe Quran is the truth from Allah, and everything revealed in it is the truth.\nReciting the Quran at a slower pace helps to reflect on it.\nThe stages of elevating with the Quran are: Slow recital, reflection, prostration with supplication, and fear with weeping.\nrefl\nوَقُرۡءَانٗا فَرَقۡنَٰهُ لِتَقۡرَأَهُۥ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ عَلَىٰ مُكۡثٖ\n(Revealed over stages), so that they may ponder and reflect upon its meanings, and derive knowledge from it. Al-Saadi: 468.\nWhat is the ideal way to recite the Quran for one who wants to reflect on it?\nقُلۡ ءَامِنُواْ بِهِۦٓ أَوۡ لَا تُؤۡمِنُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ مِن قَبۡلِهِۦٓ إِذَا يُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ يَخِرُّونَۤ لِلۡأَذۡقَانِۤ سُجَّدٗاۤ ١٠٧\n(Say, \"Believe in it or do not believe\"): This is an order to disregard them as if saying: whether you believe in it or not, for your action is not a proof; the proof lies with those who were given knowledge before it, specifically the believers among the people of the Book. (Indeed, those who were given knowledge before it), the believers from among Jews and Christians; it is also said that they were those who followed Abraham (u) before the coming of Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ). Ibn Juzay: 1/499.\nThis verse indicates the high status of scholars, Explain.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ مِن قَبۡلِهِۦٓ إِذَا يُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ يَخِرُّونَۤ لِلۡأَذۡقَانِۤ سُجَّدٗاۤ ١٠٧ وَيَقُولُونَ سُبۡحَٰنَ رَبِّنَآ إِن كَانَ وَعۡدُ رَبِّنَا لَمَفۡعُولٗا ١٠٨ وَيَخِرُّونَ لِلۡأَذۡقَانِ يَبۡكُونَ وَيَزِيدُهُمۡ خُشُوعٗا۩ ١٠٩\n(And they fall upon their faces weeping), this is praise for the scholars, and whoever is given knowledge should strive to attain this status by feeling humility when listening to the Quran and humbling himself. In Sunan ad-Darimi, Al-Taimi said: \"Whoever is given knowledge that does not cause him to weep, should not have been given that knowledge because Allah describes the scholars like this,\" then he recited this verse. Al-Qurtubi: 13/189.\nExplain how scholars should feel when listening to the Quran.\nوَيَخِرُّونَ لِلۡأَذۡقَانِ يَبۡكُونَ وَيَزِيدُهُمۡ خُشُوعٗا۩ ١٠٩\nFalling upon their faces is an act of worship that is loved by Allah. It does not mean touching the ground with their chins like they do with their foreheads; falling upon the face begins with bowing and ends with prostration. Ibn Taimyah: 4/249.\nWhat is the form of falling upon the face that is loved by Allah?\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنزَلَ عَلَىٰ عَبۡدِهِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ\nAllah praises Himself, which is an implicit instruction to people to praise Him for sending the Messenger (ﷺ) to them and sending down the Book to them. Al-Saadi: 469.\nWhat is the practical benefit for a Muslim to know that Allah praises Himself?\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنزَلَ عَلَىٰ عَبۡدِهِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَلَمۡ يَجۡعَل لَّهُۥ عِوَجَاۜ ١\nAllah singles out His Messenger (ﷺ) for mention because sending down the Quran upon him was a special favor upon him and a general one upon all people. Al-Baghawi: 3/5.\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) is singled out for mention. Why?\nقَيِّمٗا لِّيُنذِرَ بَأۡسٗا شَدِيدٗا مِّن لَّدُنۡهُ وَيُبَشِّرَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ أَنَّ لَهُمۡ أَجۡرًا حَسَنٗا ٢ مَّٰكِثِينَ فِيهِ أَبَدٗا ٣\nThis Quran refers to every good deed that leads to what brings joy to the heart. Al-Saadi: 470.\nWhat is the source of joy for the believer?\nwords\nفَرَقنَاهُWe thoroughly explained it to separate truth from falsehood\nمُكثٍA slower pace\nيَخِرُّونَ لِلأَذقَانِThey fall upon their faces in prostration\nوَلا تُخَافِتAnd do not recite too quietly in your prayer\nعِوَجًاA deviance from truth\nمِن لَدُنهُFrom Him"],[294,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm on Your religion.\"\nToday, say this supplication often:\nToday, plan to acquire good companions who will help you in worshiping Allah and being steadfast in religion.\nguid\nThis verse shows the great compassion of the Prophet (ﷺ) toward the people so that they accept Islam to the point of grieving himself to death.\nBeware! The blessings and worldly pleasures are a trial from Allah because you can use them in obeying as well as disobeying Him.\nThe righteous companionship is a cause for guidance and steadfastness in religion.\nrefl\nفَلَعَلَّكَ بَٰخِعٞ نَّفۡسَكَ عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَٰرِهِمۡ إِن لَّمۡ يُؤۡمِنُواْ بِهَٰذَا ٱلۡحَدِيثِ أَسَفًا ٦\nThere is a lesson in this and similar verses: the one who is required to call people to Allah must convey the message and strive by all possible means to guide them and block the path of misguidance as much as he can, while putting his trust in Allah. Then, if they are guided, all is well and good; otherwise, he should not grieve or feel sad, for that weakens one's resolve and saps one’s strength, and there is no benefit in it. Rather, he should carry on and persist in doing what he is required to do and aimed for, as anything other than that is beyond his means. Al-Saadi: 470.\nThis verse contains a valuable lesson for a preacher to Allah. Explain.\nإِنَّا جَعَلۡنَا مَا عَلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ زِينَةٗ لَّهَا لِنَبۡلُوَهُمۡ أَيُّهُمۡ أَحۡسَنُ عَمَلٗا ٧\n(We have made all that is on earth as an adornment for it), what is fit for adornment such as clothing, foods, trees, and rivers, etc. (So that We may test them as to which of them is best in deeds) to test them as to which of them will be less inclined toward the adornment of this world. Ibn Juzay: 1/502.\nAllah made all kinds of adornment to this life for a great wisdom. What is it?\nأَمۡ حَسِبۡتَ أَنَّ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡكَهۡفِ وَٱلرَّقِيمِ كَانُواْ مِنۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا عَجَبًا ٩ إِذۡ أَوَى ٱلۡفِتۡيَةُ إِلَى ٱلۡكَهۡفِ فَقَالُواْ رَبَّنَآ ءَاتِنَا مِن لَّدُنكَ رَحۡمَةٗ وَهَيِّئۡ لَنَا مِنۡ أَمۡرِنَا رَشَدٗا ١٠\nThis verse re-directs the attention of those who are preoccupied with wonderous stories to being admonished and drawing lessons from their causes and consequences. That is why Allah begins by mentioning the state in which they were, (when the youths took refuge in the Cave, and said, \"Our Lord, grant us mercy from Yourself, and show us the right way in our ordeal\"). Ibn Ashur: 15/259.\nAttention should be directed to the admonishments and lessons from the stories rather than their wonders. How can you infer that from the presentation of the story of the people of the Cave?\nإِذۡ أَوَى ٱلۡفِتۡيَةُ إِلَى ٱلۡكَهۡفِ فَقَالُواْ رَبَّنَآ ءَاتِنَا مِن لَّدُنكَ رَحۡمَةٗ وَهَيِّئۡ لَنَا مِنۡ أَمۡرِنَا رَشَدٗا ١٠\nThis verse provides a clear proof of allowing fleeing for the sake of religion and leaving family, sons, relatives, friends, homes, and wealth behind for fear of persecution and adversity. The Prophet (ﷺ) migrated for the sake of religion, and so did his Companions. They left their homes, land, families, sons, relatives, and brothers in order to be safe with their religion from the persecution of the disbelievers. Al-Qurtubi: 13/216.\nShould the believer leave his homeland when he fears for his religion? Or should he stays and risks his religion?\nإِنَّهُمۡ فِتۡيَةٌ ءَامَنُواْ بِرَبِّهِمۡ وَزِدۡنَٰهُمۡ هُدٗى ١٣\nAllah states that they were boys, young men; they were more accepting of the truth and more inclined to guidance than the elders, who had become stubbornly set in their ways and clung to the religion of falsehood. For the same reason, most of those who responded to Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) were young people. As for the elders of Quraish, most of them remained on their religion and only a few of them became Muslims. Ibn Kathir: 3/72.\nPeople who are likely to accept the truth belong usually to which age group?\nوَرَبَطۡنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ\nMeaning: We strengthened their hearts with patience, kept them firm, and secured them with the light of faith, so they became determined to migrate from the land of their people, leave their lavish and plentiful life behind, and head toward the Cave for the sake of their religion. Al-Baghawi: 3/17.\nHow did Allah strengthen the hearts of the people of the Cave?\nوَرَبَطۡنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ\nStrengthening the heart is the opposite of forsaking. Forsaking means removing the heart from the path of success, causing one to become heedless of Allah's remembrance, and follow his desire, which leads to the loss of his affairs. Strengthening the heart is binding it with the means of success, so the believer remembers Allah, and follows what pleases Him, so his affairs become sound. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/157.\nIn light of this pause, explain the difference between strengthening the heart and forsaking it.\nwords\nبَاخِعٌkilling\nأَسَفًاGrief\nوَالرَّقِيمِA tablet on which their names were inscribed\nأَمَدًاA time span\nشَطَطًاA transgression too far away from the truth"],[295,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nprepare a list of food items from the best Halal food, and stay away from the unlawful and doubtful items, as this sets right your heart, empowers your brain and makes your supplication more likely to be answered.\nTrue guidance comes only from Allah, so ask Him for it, and seek refuge with Him from misguidance and going astray.\nDo not wish for an encounter with the enemy, and pray to Allah to grant you safety in your faith and life.\nguid\nAllah has protected His allies in their sleep, will He not protect them while awake?!\nThe good Halal food has many benefits; it is a cause for guidance, a cause for answering supplication and keeps diseases away.\nWhen a believer is cautious about the enmity of the disbelievers, he will be safe from their evil.\nrefl\nوَإِذِ ٱعۡتَزَلۡتُمُوهُمۡ وَمَا يَعۡبُدُونَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ\nIt was said that when they called their king to believe in Allah, he refused, warned and threatened them. He gave them respite to think about the situation, hoping that they would return to their former religion. During that respite, they managed to escape from him and flee from persecution for the sake of their religion. In such cases, it is allowed to seclude oneself from people, but this is not prescribed in any other case, because by such seclusion one loses the benefits of congregational and Friday prayers. Ibn Kathir: 3/73.\nWhen is it allowed for a Muslim to seclude himself and flee from people for the sake of his religion?\nوَتَرَى ٱلشَّمۡسَ إِذَا طَلَعَت تَّزَٰوَرُ عَن كَهۡفِهِمۡ ذَاتَ ٱلۡيَمِينِ وَإِذَا غَرَبَت تَّقۡرِضُهُمۡ ذَاتَ ٱلشِّمَالِ وَهُمۡ فِي فَجۡوَةٖ مِّنۡهُۚ ذَٰلِكَ مِنۡ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِۗ\nMeaning: The sun did not shine on them when it rose nor when it set so that they would not be burned by its heat. It is said that this was a signs of honor and a miraculous event. Ibn Juzay: 1/504.\nHow did Allah protect the people of the Cave?\nمَن يَهۡدِ ٱللَّهُ فَهُوَ ٱلۡمُهۡتَدِۖ\nMeaning: There is no way to attain guidance except from Allah, for He guides to all that is best in both realms [this world and the Hereafter]. Al-Saadi: 472.\nFrom whom should you ask for guidance when you want it?\nوَنُقَلِّبُهُمۡ ذَاتَ ٱلۡيَمِينِ وَذَاتَ ٱلشِّمَالِۖ\nThis was also to protect their bodies, for the earth naturally consumes bodies that are in direct contact with it. But by the decree of Allah, He caused them to turn over to their right and left sides, as much as was needed to prevent the earth causing damage to their bodies. Allah was able to protect them from the earth without turning them over, but He is Most Wise, and He wanted His universal laws to be consistent and for causes and effects to remain in place. Al-Saadi: 472.\nAllah was able to protect them from the earth without turning them over, why did He make the turn over?\nوَكَلۡبُهُم بَٰسِطٞ ذِرَاعَيۡهِ بِٱلۡوَصِيدِۚ\nIbn Atiyah said: I said: 'If a dog had attained this high rank by joining the righteous and allies of Allah to the point that Allah is mentioning it in His Book, then what do you think about the believers who join and love the righteous and allies of Allah.\" Al-Qurtubi: 13/232.\nWhat do we learn from the mention of the dog in this story?\nقَالُواْ رَبُّكُمۡ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا لَبِثۡتُمۡ\nThe proper etiquette to follow in the event of being uncertain about an issue of knowledge is to refer it to someone who knows about it, and one should not go beyond what he knows. Al-Saadi: 473.\nWhat is the Islamic etiquette to follow when being asked about unknown issue to you?\nفَلۡيَنظُرۡ أَيُّهَآ أَزۡكَىٰ طَعَامٗا فَلۡيَأۡتِكُم بِرِزۡقٖ مِّنۡهُ\nIt is permissible to eat good and delicious food, so long as that does not go to the extent of extravagance that is prohibited. This applies, especially, if a person is used to that and nothing else will suit him. Al-Saadi: 473.\nIs man enjoined to stay away from the best food?\nwords\nمِرفَقًاWhat you will need of provision, dwelling\nتَزَاوَرُIt would incline away\nتَقرِضُهُمIt would turn away from them\nفَجوَةٍAn open space"],[296,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nRemember Allah, the Almighty, often today.\nStarting today, ensure that every time you speak about future plans to say, \"If Allah wills\".\nRecite a Surah from the Quran.\nguid\nSentiment and enthusiasm for doing good deeds are not enough, for adherence to the rules of Sharia is an obligation. Building Mosques at grave sites is prohibited.\nDo not engage in an argument unless you have the proper knowledge.\nWhenever you need a Fatwa, look for the best scholar in his worship and knowledge.\nrefl\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَعۡثَرۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ لِيَعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّٞ وَأَنَّ ٱلسَّاعَةَ لَا رَيۡبَ فِيهَآ\nThis story proves that whoever flees persecution for the sake of his religion, Allah will protect him from that; whoever strives to maintain his well-being, Allah will grant him that; whoever seeks refuge with Allah, Allah will grant him refuge and cause him to be a means of guidance for others; whoever puts up with humiliation for Allah's sake, seeking His pleasure, the ultimate consequences will be high status for him that will be achieved in a manner that he does not expect. Al-Saadi: 473.\nList three useful lessons from the story of the people of the cave.\nفَقَالُواْ ٱبۡنُواْ عَلَيۡهِم بُنۡيَٰنٗاۖ رَّبُّهُمۡ أَعۡلَمُ بِهِمۡۚ قَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ غَلَبُواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَمۡرِهِمۡ لَنَتَّخِذَنَّ عَلَيۡهِم مَّسۡجِدٗا ٢١\nBuilding mosques at grave sites and praying at them is prohibited because that is a pretense for worshiping the dead, or similar to the actions of some who worship their righteous dead people. Ibn Ashur: 15/290.\nBuilding Mosques at graves sites is prohibited. Why?\nقُل رَّبِّيٓ أَعۡلَمُ بِعِدَّتِهِم\nThis indicates that the best thing to do in matters like this is to refer knowledge to Allah, because there is no need to indulge in discussing such matters without knowledge. If we are given knowledge of a matter, then we may talk about it; otherwise, we should refrain. Ibn Kathir: 3/77.\nWhen a student of knowledge is questioned about unknown issues to him, what is the best thing for him to do?\nوَلَا تَسۡتَفۡتِ فِيهِم مِّنۡهُمۡ أَحَدٗا ٢٢\nThis proves that it is not allowed to seek Fatwas from someone who is not fit to issue Fatwas, either because he does not have sufficient knowledge concerning the issue in question, or because he is careless in his talk and may give any answer. This verse also indicates that it may be forbidden to ask a person about some things and not other things, so he may be asked about that of which he has knowledge, but not other matters, because Allah did not forbid us to ask them questions in all cases; rather, He only forbade us to ask them about the story of the people of the Cave and similar matters. Al-Saadi: 474.\nMention some of the issues related to Fatwa, which are derived from this verse?\nوَلَا تَقُولَنَّ لِشَاْيۡءٍ إِنِّي فَاعِلٞ ذَٰلِكَ غَدًا ٢٣ إِلَّا أَن يَشَآءَ ٱللَّهُۚ\nMeaning: If you intend to do something in the future, do not say, \"I will do this tomorrow\" unless you say, \"If Allah wills.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/23.\nWhat is the Quranic guidance to what must one say if he wants to do something in the future?\nوَٱذۡكُر رَّبَّكَ إِذَا نَسِيتَ\nThis is guidance to anyone who forgets something in his speech. It is important to remember Allah, as forgetfulness comes from the devil, and the remembrance of Allah drives away the devil, so when the devil is gone, forgetfulness is eliminated. The remembrance of Allah is a cause for remembering. Ibn Kathir: 3/78.\nWhat is the link between remembering Allah and ridding forgetfulness?\nمَا لَهُم مِّن دُونِهِۦ مِن وَلِيّٖ وَلَا يُشۡرِكُ فِي حُكۡمِهِۦٓ أَحَدٗا ٢٦\nA protector (an ally) is one whom you have a reason on which an alliance between you and him is based. Faith is the reason for which the believers are allies of their Lord through obedience, and He is their ally by rewarding, empowering and helping them. Al-Shanqiti: 3/257.\nAllah is the ally of the believers, and they are allies of Him. Explain.\nwords\nأَعثَرنَا عَلَيهِمWe made their case known to the people\nلا رَيبَNo doubt\nغَلَبُوا عَلَى أَمرِهِمThose who prevailed in their matter\nرَجمًا بِالغَيبِGuessing at the unseen\nفَلاَ تُمَارِ فِيهِمSo do not argue about their number\nإلَّا مِرَاءً ظَاهِرًاExcept with an obvious argument\nمُلتَحَدًاA refuge"],[297,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nPartake in a program for inviting others to Allah with a group of righteous people.\nLook for a righteous person, befriend him and be patient with him for the sake of Allah.\nSeek refuge with Allah from becoming arrogant because of the favors He bestowed upon you, and ask Him to help you use them in His worship.\nguid\nSet for yourself a daily remembrance of Allah in the morning and evening.\nSeek the companionship of righteous people, and strive to be with them even if they are poor, and beware of being distracted away from them by the adornments of this worldly life.\nAmong the worst punishments for some of your sins is making your heart heedless of the remembrance of Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱصۡبِرۡ نَفۡسَكَ مَعَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلۡغَدَوٰةِ وَٱلۡعَشِيِّ يُرِيدُونَ وَجۡهَهُۥۖ وَلَا تَعۡدُ عَيۡنَاكَ عَنۡهُمۡ تُرِيدُ زِينَةَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ وَلَا تُطِعۡ مَنۡ أَغۡفَلۡنَا قَلۡبَهُۥ عَن ذِكۡرِنَا وَٱتَّبَعَ هَوَىٰهُ وَكَانَ أَمۡرُهُۥ فُرُطٗا ٢٨\n(And be patient), stay put in patience (with those who call upon their Lord), the poor among Muslims, such as Bilal, Khabbab, and Suhaib. The disbelievers said to the Prophet (ﷺ): \"Drive these people away, and we will sit with you.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/507.\nThe preacher deals with various types of people, what is the Quranic guidance for that?\nوَٱصۡبِرۡ نَفۡسَكَ مَعَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلۡغَدَوٰةِ وَٱلۡعَشِيِّ يُرِيدُونَ وَجۡهَهُۥۖ\nThis verse indicates the importance of remembering Allah, calling upon Him and worshiping Him at both ends of the day. Moreover, Allah praises those who are engaged in this action, and whenever Allah praises someone of an action, it signifies His love for that. Thus, if Allah loves it, then He enjoins it, and encourages people to do it. Al-Saadi: 475.\nHow do you infer from this verse the validity of Athkar in the morning and evening?\nوَلَا تَعۡدُ عَيۡنَاكَ عَنۡهُمۡ تُرِيدُ زِينَةَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ\n(Desiring the adornment of the life of this world), for that is harmful and of no benefit, and it may undermine one's religious interests because it leads to being attached to this world and focusing one's ideas and thoughts on it, which leads to the heart losing interest in the Hereafter. That is because the adornment of this world is pleasing to the onlooker and bewitches the mind, which in turn distracts the heart from the remembrance of Allah and causes it to focus on pleasures and desires that waste his time and cause his affairs to be in disarray. Al-Saadi: 475.\nWhat is the harm in preferring this worldly life over the Hereafter?\nوَلَا تُطِعۡ مَنۡ أَغۡفَلۡنَا قَلۡبَهُۥ عَن ذِكۡرِنَا وَٱتَّبَعَ هَوَىٰهُ وَكَانَ أَمۡرُهُۥ فُرُطٗا ٢٨\nThis verse indicates that the one who should be obeyed and should be a leader of people is one whose heart is filled with love for Allah, and that is reflected in his speech, so he constantly remembers Allah and seeks the pleasure of his Lord, and he gives precedence to that over his desires. By doing so, he makes the most of his time; his affairs are in order, his deeds are righteous, and he calls people to what Allah has blessed him with. Thus, he deserves to be followed and to be made a leader. Al-Saadi: 475.\nIt is inevitable for one to follow others in some religious or worldly issues, who must we follow? And who must we avoid?\nوَقُلِ ٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكُمۡۖ فَمَن شَآءَ فَلۡيُؤۡمِن وَمَن شَآءَ فَلۡيَكۡفُرۡۚ\nMeaning: Allah grants truth to whomever He wills, even if he is weak, and deprives of the truth whomever He wills, even if he is rich and powerful; hence, I will not drive away the believers for your sake, so, believe, if you will, or disbelieve. Al-Qurtubi: 13/260.\nDoes one's financial status affect Allah's favors that are in the Hereafter?\nوَقُلِ ٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكُمۡۖ فَمَن شَآءَ فَلۡيُؤۡمِن وَمَن شَآءَ فَلۡيَكۡفُرۡۚ\nIn this verse, belief precedes disbelief since their belief is sought after. Ibn Ashur: 15/307.\nIn this verse, belief precedes disbelief. Why?\nوَكَانَ لَهُۥ ثَمَرٞ فَقَالَ لِصَٰحِبِهِۦ وَهُوَ يُحَاوِرُهُۥٓ أَنَا۠ أَكۡثَرُ مِنكَ مَالٗا وَأَعَزُّ نَفَرٗا ٣٤\nQatadah said: \"This, by Allah, is the wish of the immoral to have much wealth and a large entourage.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/81.\nWhat is ultimate wish of the disbeliever? How should the Muslim benefit from that?\nwords\nفُرُطًاAt a loss\nسُرَادِقُهَاIts wall\nكَالمُهلِLike a murky oil\nوَسَاءَت مُرتَفَقاًWhat a terrible resting place\nسُندُسٍFine silk\nوَإِستَبرَقٍThick silk"],[298,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nGive advice to a friend of yours who disobeys Allah and His Messenger. Friendship should not prevent advising each other.\nReflect on some of your achievements in life, give the credit for them to Allah and say, \"This is by Allah's Will; there is no power except with Allah.\".\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness for giving yourself the credit for a blessing while forgetting to give the credit to Allah. Allah's punishment is close to a person who is heedless of being grateful to Him.\nguid\nBeware of boasting and feeling secure from the plan of Allah.\nWhoever is forsaken by Allah, will never be helped.\nBe humble with the servants of Allah, and beware of arrogance and feeling superior.\nrefl\nوَدَخَلَ جَنَّتَهُۥ وَهُوَ ظَالِمٞ لِّنَفۡسِهِۦ قَالَ مَآ أَظُنُّ أَن تَبِيدَ هَٰذِهِۦٓ أَبَدٗا ٣٥\n(While he was unjust to himself), either by his disbelief or by his encounter with his companion, since he showed boasting, arrogance, and disdain for him. Ibn Juzay: 1/510.\nThe garden's owner was unjust to himself by committing four things. What were they?\nوَلَئِن رُّدِدتُّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّي لَأَجِدَنَّ خَيۡرٗا مِّنۡهَا مُنقَلَبٗا ٣٦\nWhat connection can there be between what one is given in this world and what he will be given in the Hereafter, such that one might think, on the basis of ignorance, that the one who is given bounty in this world will necessarily be given bounty in the hereafter? Rather, what is usually the case is that Allah keeps worldly gains away from His allies and chosen ones, while granting such things in abundance to His enemies, who have no share in the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 477.\nIs there a connection between what one is given in this world and what he will be given in the Hereafter?\nوَلَوۡلَآ إِذۡ دَخَلۡتَ جَنَّتَكَ قُلۡتَ مَا شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَا قُوَّةَ إِلَّا بِٱللَّهِۚ\nMeaning: Whatever wealth that had been accumulated for you was solely by the might and power of Allah, not by your own, and if He wills, He would remove His blessing from it, rendering it nothing at all. Al-Qurtubi: 13/280.\nCan man own anything with his own power?\nإِن تَرَنِ أَنَا۠ أَقَلَّ مِنكَ مَالٗا وَوَلَدٗا ٣٩ فَعَسَىٰ رَبِّيٓ أَن يُؤۡتِيَنِ خَيۡرٗا مِّن جَنَّتِكَ\nThe believer said to his disbelieving companion that Allah's blessing of faith and Islam upon him -even with little wealth and fewer sons- is the true blessing while everything else is subject to termination and punishment. Al-Saadi: 477.\nWhat are the best and most complete blessing upon the Muslim?\nوَأُحِيطَ بِثَمَرِهِۦ فَأَصۡبَحَ يُقَلِّبُ كَفَّيۡهِ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَنفَقَ فِيهَا وَهِيَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلَىٰ عُرُوشِهَا\nThe punishment that destroyed his garden was not for his disbelief; rather, Allah may give many disbelievers enjoyment throughout life, give them respite, and gradually lead them to their demise. However, the swift punishment of this disbeliever was due to his tyranny, and the use of his wealth as a means to disdain the poor believer. Ibn Ashur: 15/328.\nWhat was the reason for the swift punishment of this disbeliever who is mentioned in this verse even though Allah may give many disbelievers enjoyment throughout life?\nوَيَقُولُ يَٰلَيۡتَنِي لَمۡ أُشۡرِكۡ بِرَبِّيٓ أَحَدٗا ٤٢\nIt is not implausible to say that by the mercy and kindness of Allah, the situation of this owner of the garden that was destroyed later improved, and Allah enabled him to turn back to Him, come back to his senses, and give up his rebellion and transgression. That is based on the fact that he expressed regret for his ascription of partners to his Lord, and that Allah took away from him what had caused him to transgress, and He punished him in this world. If Allah wills good for a person, He hastens to punish him in this world. Al-Saadi: 478.\nThe punishment of the garden's owner may had been good for him. Explain.\nوَٱضۡرِبۡ لَهُم مَّثَلَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا كَمَآءٍ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ فَٱخۡتَلَطَ بِهِۦ نَبَاتُ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَأَصۡبَحَ هَشِيمٗا تَذۡرُوهُ ٱلرِّيَٰحُۗ\nWise men said: Allah likens this life to water because water does not stay in one form, and so does this life. Water does not last but disappears, and this life also terminates. Every one who enters water becomes wet, and the same happens with one who is in this life, where he cannot escape its temptations and troubles. A reasonable amount of water is useful, while more of it is harmful, and the same can be said about this life, having what suffices is useful while taking excess is harmful. Al-Qurtubi: 13/289.\nExplain some of the similarities between water and the life of this world.\nwords\nتَبِيدَPerishes\nصَعِيدًا زَلَقًاA smooth barren land\nغَورًاSeeps deep in the ground"],[299,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to grant you soundness of the heart, and seek refuge with Him from envy and arrogance, as theses two sins had doomed the devil.\nIdentify sins you had committed that you believe they were major sins, and ask for Allah's forgiveness often so that they may be deleted from your record of deeds.\nSettle on a major righteous endeavor to be your lifetime project, then begin taking serious steps toward its realization while seeking Allah's help so you would not live in heedlessness.\nguid\nDo not let your wealth and children distract you from doing righteous deeds, but let them be a means to doing that.\nWhoever keeps count of his good and bad deeds, will not be stunned by his record of deeds on the Day of Resurrection.\nOn the Day of the Resurrection, the polytheist's greatest regret will be finding out that no one can be a partner with Allah in relieving an affliction or answering a prayer.\nrefl\nٱلۡمَالُ وَٱلۡبَنُونَ زِينَةُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ\nWealth and children) which Utbah bin Rabi'ah (one of the chiefs of Quraish) and his rich fellows used to brag about are (the adornments of the life of this world) and not among the provisions of the Hereafter. Ali bin Abi Talib (t) said: \"Wealth and children are the harvest [benefits] of this world while righteous deeds are the harvest of the Hereafter, and Allah may combine both for some people.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/34.\nWhat is the harvest of this world? And what is the harvest of the Hereafter?\nوَٱلۡبَٰقِيَٰتُ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ خَيۡرٌ عِندَ رَبِّكَ ثَوَابٗا وَخَيۡرٌ أَمَلٗا ٤٦\nWhat will remain and benefit a person, bringing him joy, are righteous deeds of lasting merit. That includes all acts of obedience, both obligatory and recommended, having to do with the rights of Allah and the rights of His servants, such as Prayer, Zakah, Charity, Hajj, Umrah, Tasbeeh, Tahmeed, Tahleel, Takbeer, reciting Quran, seeking beneficial knowledge, enjoining what is right, forbidding what is wrong, maintaining ties of kinship, honoring one's parents, fulfilling the rights of wives, slaves, and animals, and all acts of kindness toward people. Al-Saadi: 479.\nList some of the lasting righteous deeds.\nوَتَرَى ٱلۡأَرۡضَ بَارِزَةٗ\nMeaning: Clear and open, with no features that anyone may recognize and nothing for anyone to hide behind. All creatures will be visible to their Lord, and not one of them will be hidden from Him. Ibn Kathir: 3/85-86.\n(And you will see the earth laid bare) implies a warning, what is it about?\nلَّقَدۡ جِئۡتُمُونَا كَمَا خَلَقۡنَٰكُمۡ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةِۚ\nMeaning: Without wealth, without family and without tribe. They will have nothing with them except the deeds that they did and whatever they earned of good or evil. Al-Saadi: 479.\nWhat is meant by (You have certainly come to Us just as We created you the first time)?\nوَيَقُولُونَ يَٰوَيۡلَتَنَا مَالِ هَٰذَا ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَا يُغَادِرُ صَغِيرَةٗ وَلَا كَبِيرَةً إِلَّآ أَحۡصَىٰهَاۚ وَوَجَدُواْ مَا عَمِلُواْ حَاضِرٗاۗ وَلَا يَظۡلِمُ رَبُّكَ أَحَدٗا ٤٩\nQatadah said: They will complain about the enumeration, and no one will ever complain about injustice, so beware of evil deeds that are regarded as insignificant, for when they are accumulated, they destroy their perpetrator. Al-Qurtubi: 15/459.\nWhen will the servant likely be destroyed by insignificant sins?\nوَإِذۡ قُلۡنَا لِلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ ٱسۡجُدُواْ لِأٓدَمَ\nA prostration of respect and honor. Ibn Kathir: 3/87.\nWas the prostration of angels to Adam (u) an act of worship? What was it?.\nوَإِذۡ قُلۡنَا لِلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ ٱسۡجُدُواْ لِأٓدَمَ فَسَجَدُوٓاْ إِلَّآ إِبۡلِيسَ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡجِنِّ فَفَسَقَ عَنۡ أَمۡرِ رَبِّهِۦٓۗ أَفَتَتَّخِذُونَهُۥ وَذُرِّيَّتَهُۥٓ أَوۡلِيَآءَ مِن دُونِي وَهُمۡ لَكُمۡ عَدُوُّۢۚ بِئۡسَ لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ بَدَلٗا ٥٠\nAllah points out to the children of Adam the enmity of Iblis toward them and their father before them, and rebukes those who follow him and go against their Creator and Master. It is He who created them from nothing and sustains and nourishes them by His kindness, yet they still took Iblis as their ally and declared their enmity toward Allah. So Allah says, (And [mention] when We said to the angels). Ibn Kathir: 3/87.\nExplain some of the ignorance and stubbornness of the children of Adam in light of this verse.\nwords\nوَخَيرٌ أَمَلًاAnd better in hope for Allah's reward\nفَفَسَقَHe disobeyed\nعَضُدًاHelpers\nمَوبِقًاA valley of destruction in Hell"],[300,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nRead one story from Surat Al-Kahf, and reflect on its lessons and admonitions.\nIdentify one of the reasons for your heedlessness, begin serious steps to leave it, and ask Allah to give you something much better instead.\nVisit a scholar and learn some of his knowledge, read a book to him, or learn from his mannerism and dignified style.\nguid\nArguing and quarreling are intrinsic to man, so one should tame and direct them toward pursuing good things.\nUse the approach of endearing and intimidation when preaching to Allah.\nAllah may place coverings and veils over a sinner's heart so that he becomes unable to reflect on the Quran or understand its examples and narrations until he repents.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ صَرَّفۡنَا فِي هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ لِلنَّاسِ مِن كُلِّ مَثَلٖۚ وَكَانَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ أَكۡثَرَ شَيۡءٖ جَدَلٗا ٥٤\nIt was narrated by Ali bin Abi Talib that the Prophet (ﷺ) came to him and Fatimah at night and said: \"Will you not pray?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) our souls are in the hand of Allah, and if He wants to make us get up, He will make us get up.\" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went away when I said that to him. Then, as he was leaving, I heard him striking his thigh and saying, (but man is the most quarrelsome of all beings). Ibn Ashur: 15/348.\nWhen someone offers advice, it should be considered as much as possible. Explain\nوَكَانَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ أَكۡثَرَ شَيۡءٖ جَدَلٗا ٥٤\nMany people argue about the truth after it has become clear, and they debate on the basis of falsehood, seeking to undermine the truth. Hence, Allah says, (but man is the most quarrelsome of all beings) in debates and disputes concerning the Quran, even though that is inappropriate and unfair on his part. What cause a man to be like that and not believe in Allah is nothing other than wrongdoing and stubbornness; the lack of acceptance is not due to any deficiencies in the proof and evidence presented in the Quran. Al-Saadi: 480.\nIs arguing with scholars and students of knowledge a good thing? What is the reason that makes one argue much with people of truth?.\nوَمَا نُرۡسِلُ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ إِلَّا مُبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنذِرِينَۚ وَيُجَٰدِلُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ لِيُدۡحِضُواْ بِهِ ٱلۡحَقَّۖ وَٱتَّخَذُوٓاْ ءَايَٰتِي وَمَآ أُنذِرُواْ هُزُوٗا ٥٦\nAllah differentiates between the signs (verses) that point to the knowledge, which are the proofs of the Lord, and the warnings that tell about the punishments, like informing the Prophets about what the disbelievers deserve of punishments. Thus, it is known by both: knowledge and warnings. Ibn Taimyah: 4/260.\nWhat is the difference between the signs and the warnings?\nوَمَا نُرۡسِلُ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ إِلَّا مُبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنذِرِينَۚ\n(And We do not send the messengers except as bearers of glad tidings) of Paradise for those who believe, and (warners) of punishment to those who disbelieve. Al-Qurtubi: 13/311.\nList two methods of preaching to Allah, which are mentioned in this verse.\nوَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّن ذُكِّرَ بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّهِۦ فَأَعۡرَضَ عَنۡهَا وَنَسِيَ مَا قَدَّمَتۡ يَدَاهُۚ إِنَّا جَعَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ أَكِنَّةً أَن يَفۡقَهُوهُ وَفِيٓ ءَاذَانِهِمۡ وَقۡرٗاۖ وَإِن تَدۡعُهُمۡ إِلَى ٱلۡهُدَىٰ فَلَن يَهۡتَدُوٓاْ إِذًا أَبَدٗا ٥٧\nThis verse is aimed at scaring those who reject the truth after having known it. It warns of a barrier that could be erected, preventing them from following it any further. Nothing is more alarming or a greater deterrent than that. Al-Saadi: 481.\nThere is a difference between one who turns away from truth while being aware of it and another who does the same while being ignorant of it. Explain that in light of this verse.\nوَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّن ذُكِّرَ بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّهِۦ فَأَعۡرَضَ عَنۡهَا وَنَسِيَ مَا قَدَّمَتۡ يَدَاهُۚ\nMeaning: No one is more unjust to himself than one who is admonished by the verses of his Lord but takes them lightly and turns away from accepting them. Al-Qurtubi: 13/312.\nAmong all people, who is the most unjust to himself?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِفَتَىٰهُ لَآ أَبۡرَحُ حَتَّىٰٓ أَبۡلُغَ مَجۡمَعَ ٱلۡبَحۡرَيۡنِ أَوۡ أَمۡضِيَ حُقُبٗا ٦٠\nThere are useful lessons in this story: A trip is taken by a scholar to seek more knowledge while being helped by a servant and a companion. Meeting up with honorable men and scholars -despite their distant places- is a custom of the righteous predecessors; hence, such travelers reached the best aim and gained a successful pursuit. So, they became firm in their knowledge and attained high honor among people and a great reward from Allah. Al-Bukhari said: \"Jaber bin Abdullah traveled for a month to meet with Abdulla bin Onais (j) to hear one Hadith from him.\" Al-Qurtubi: 13/318.\nWhat does a student of knowledge learn from Moses (u) trip to acquire knowledge?\nwords\nلِيُدحِضُواThey seek to undermine\nأَكِنَّةًCoverings\nوَقرًاDeafness, hearing loss\nمَوئِلًاAn escape\nحُقُبًاA long period"],[301,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to grant you mercy for his creation and the knowledge about the Creator, as the most knowledgeable about Allah is most merciful in dealing with His creation.\nBecoming closer to Allah can be attained through accompanying His allies which is gained through good morals.\nRead a book about the etiquettes of the student of knowledge, reflect on it and implement it.\nguid\nListening, reading and pondering are only means, and the giver of knowledge is Allah.\nA teacher may gently reproof his student to test his endurance and resolve.\nReflect on this story of the journey to seek knowledge, as it has many useful lessons.\nrefl\nءَاتِنَا غَدَآءَنَا\nIt is recommended for a person to feed his servant the same food that he himself eats, and to eat together with him, because the apparent meaning of Moses' words, (Bring us our meal), refers to both of them and suggests that they would eat together. Al-Saadi: 483.\nThe verse indicates some manners in dealing with servants. Explain.\nفَلَمَّا جَاوَزَا قَالَ لِفَتَىٰهُ ءَاتِنَا غَدَآءَنَا لَقَدۡ لَقِينَا مِن سَفَرِنَا هَٰذَا نَصَبٗا ٦٢\nThis verse proves that it is allowed for one to express what he feels of pain and diseases, and it does not contradict contentment with the decree of Allah provided that he does not show dissatisfaction. Al-Qurtubi: 13/322.\nFor one to express his situation, is that considered objection to the decree of Allah?\nوَمَآ أَنسَىٰنِيهُ إِلَّا ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَنۡ أَذۡكُرَهُۥۚ\nEvil and its causes may be ascribed to the devil because of his temptation and ability to make evil appear enticing, although all things happen by the will and decree of Allah. Al-Saadi: 483.\nForgetfulness was ascribed to the devil even though it occurred by the will of Allah. Explain.\nقَالَ لَهُۥ مُوسَىٰ هَلۡ أَتَّبِعُكَ عَلَىٰٓ أَن تُعَلِّمَنِ مِمَّا عُلِّمۡتَ رُشۡدٗا ٦٦\nThis is a question phrased in gentle terms, with no sense of force or coercion. This is the manner in which the seeker of knowledge should address the scholar. Ibn Kathir: 3/94.\nThis verse contains an etiquette that should be observed by the seeker of knowledge toward the scholar. What is it?\nقَالَ لَهُۥ مُوسَىٰ هَلۡ أَتَّبِعُكَ عَلَىٰٓ أَن تُعَلِّمَنِ مِمَّا عُلِّمۡتَ رُشۡدٗا ٦٦\nBeneficial knowledge is that which guides toward good. Any knowledge that provides guidance to the ways of goodness and warning against the ways of evil, or being a means of achieving that, are regarded as beneficial knowledge. All other knowledge is either harmful or of no benefit because Moses (u) said, (so that you may teach me some of that sound knowledge that you have been taught). Al-Saadi: 484.\nMoses (u) requested Al-Khidr to teach him sound knowledge, not just any knowledge. Why?\nقَالَ إِنَّكَ لَن تَسۡتَطِيعَ مَعِيَ صَبۡرٗا ٦٧\nHere is a fundamental principle in teaching; the teacher should alert his student of possible difficulties that he may encounter in learning, especially if acquiring such knowledge is challenging. Ibn Ashur: 15/372.\nThe verse indicates a fundamental principle in teaching. What is it?\nقَالَ إِنَّكَ لَن تَسۡتَطِيعَ مَعِيَ صَبۡرٗا ٦٧\nMeaning: You will not be able to accompany me when you see me doing things that go against your Sharia. Ibn Kathir: 3/94.\nMoses (u) could not be patient with what Al-Khidr did. Why?\nwords\nأَوَينَاWe retired\nنَبغِWe seek\nفَارتَدَّاThey returned\nخَرَقَهَاHe removed one of the ship's wooden boards\nإِمرًاA grave thing\nنُكرًاA deplorable thing"],[302,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nDo a good deed today that benefits others.\nToday, strive to prevent an injustice that is done to an oppressed or a weak person.\nAsk Allah to make your offspring righteous.\nguid\nPatience is a condition for seeking knowledge.\nThis is an example of Allah's perfect arrangement for His allies in what appears to be harmful but it is, in fact, for their good.\nThe striving of a father to be righteous is a cause for the righteousness and provision of his offspring.\nrefl\nقَالَ إِن سَأَلۡتُكَ عَن شَيۡءِۢ بَعۡدَهَا فَلَا تُصَٰحِبۡنِيۖ قَدۡ بَلَغۡتَ مِن لَّدُنِّي عُذۡرٗا ٧٦\nAt this point, Moses (u) did not use forgetfulness as an excuse, either because he did not forget or he opted for changing a deplorable thing -which was taking a human life unjustly- in fulfilling his commitment; or he may have forgotten, but did not want to repeat the same excuse. Ibn Ashur: 16/6.\nThis time, Moses (u) did not use forgetfulness as an excuse, why?\nأَمَّا ٱلسَّفِينَةُ فَكَانَتۡ لِمَسَٰكِينَ يَعۡمَلُونَ فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ فَأَرَدتُّ أَنۡ أَعِيبَهَا وَكَانَ وَرَآءَهُم مَّلِكٞ يَأۡخُذُ كُلَّ سَفِينَةٍ غَصۡبٗا ٧٩\nAnother important principle with regard to one man handling the wealth of another is that if it is done in a manner that serves the latter's interests and wards off harm, it is permissible for him to do that, even without permission, and even if that involves causing some damage to the property of the other person, such as when Al-Khidr scuttled the ship in order to render it defective, so that it would be safe from being seized unlawfully by the unjust king. Based on that, if a fire or flood or the like occurs in the house or property o f a man, then it is permissible to damage part of the property or demolish part of the house for the sake of saving the rest. In fact, that is prescribed to protect the wealth and property of the other person. Al-Saadi: 485.\nScholars inferred an important principle from this verse, what is it?\nوَأَمَّا ٱلۡغُلَٰمُ فَكَانَ أَبَوَاهُ مُؤۡمِنَيۡنِ فَخَشِينَآ أَن يُرۡهِقَهُمَا طُغۡيَٰنٗا وَكُفۡرٗا ٨٠\nQatadah said: \"His parents rejoiced when he was born, and grieved for him when he was killed. If he had stayed alive, he would have been the cause of their doom. So, let a man be content with the decree of Allah, for the decree of Allah for the believer, if he dislikes it, is better for him than if He were to decree something that he likes for him.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/96.\nHow should the Muslim deal with griefs and afflictions?\nوَكَانَ أَبُوهُمَا صَٰلِحٗا فَأَرَادَ رَبُّكَ أَن يَبۡلُغَآ أَشُدَّهُمَا وَيَسۡتَخۡرِجَا كَنزَهُمَا\nThis Indicates that a righteous person's offspring will be taken care of, and that the blessing of his worship will extend to them in this world and in the Hereafter. This will occur through his intercession for them, as well as, their status being raised to the highest levels of Paradise, so he will be comforted by seeing them. Ibn Kathir: 3/97.\nYour righteousness may benefit your offspring. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَكَانَ أَبُوهُمَا صَٰلِحٗا فَأَرَادَ رَبُّكَ أَن يَبۡلُغَآ أَشُدَّهُمَا وَيَسۡتَخۡرِجَا كَنزَهُمَا\nThis indicates that Allah protects the righteous person and his offspring, even if they are far away from him. It is narrated that Allah protects the offspring of a righteous person up to seven generations. Al-Qurtubi: 13/356.\nWhat is the immediate reward for a person's righteousness?\nفَأَرَادَ رَبُّكَ أَن يَبۡلُغَآ أَشُدَّهُمَا وَيَسۡتَخۡرِجَا كَنزَهُمَا رَحۡمَةٗ مِّن رَّبِّكَۚ\n(So your Lord willed), he attributed the will here to Allah since it is part of the unseen which is known only to Allah. However, Al-Khidr attributed the will to himself when damaging the ship, (I wanted to make it defective), since harm is not attributed to Allah out of reverence for Him. This is similar to what Abraham (u) said, (and when I am ill, it is He who cures me) [26:80]. Ibn Juzay: 1/518.\nAl-Khidr attributed the will to himself when damaging the ship, but attributed the will to Allah when mending the wall. Why?\nوَمَا فَعَلۡتُهُۥ عَنۡ أَمۡرِيۚ ذَٰلِكَ تَأۡوِيلُ مَا لَمۡ تَسۡطِع عَّلَيۡهِ صَبۡرٗا ٨٢\n(I did not do it of my own accord) not my choice and view, rather, I did it by the command of Allah. Al-Baghawi: 3/55.\nDoes a scholar do what he wants, or follows and adheres to the command of Allah?\nwords\nاستَطعَمَا أَهلَهَاThey asked its people for food\nيُرِيدُ أَن يَنقَضَّA wall about to collapse\nبِتَأوِيلِOf the interpretation, outcome\nيُرهِقَهُمَاHe would overburden them\nزَكَاةًRighteousness, purity\nوَأَقرَبَ رُحمًاTender-hearted, nearer to mercy\nذِي القَرنَينِA righteous and just king who ruled over the area between the East and West"],[303,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nDraw three lessons from the story of Thul-Qarnayn.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the trial of Gog and Magog.\nHelp a weak or a needy person today.\nguid\nAdvise people when you see evil, falsehood or corruption.\nBe grateful to Allah always, no matter how great your power, wealth and authority are.\nGreat endeavors are handled through collaboration among people; some with their knowledge, others with their wealth, and some others with their efforts.\nrefl\nإِنَّا مَكَّنَّا لَهُۥ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ مِن كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ سَبَبٗا ٨٤\nThis story indicates four clear traits of Thul-Qarnayn, first: He was a righteous and a just ruler. Second: He has an inspiration from Allah. Third: His kingdom was spread over large regions. Fourth: His conquests toward the west had reached an unknown place called: A hot spring of black muddy water. Ibn Ashur: 16/20.\nAllah may combine for a servant the blessings of this world and the Hereafter. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ مِن كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ سَبَبٗا ٨٤\nAllah does not detail what these means that He had given him were, and His Messenger (ﷺ) does not either. There are no reports that could give us any information regarding that. Therefore, we cannot but keep quiet about them. Al-Saadi: 485.\nWhat should be our attitude toward the things of which Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) did not mention?\nوَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ مِن كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ سَبَبٗا ٨٤ فَأَتۡبَعَ سَبَبًا ٨٥\nHe used the means that Allah had given him in a proper manner. Not everyone who has means available to him uses those means, and not everyone is able to use the means available to him. If one has the true means of achieving something and uses them, his goal will be attained, but if both factors -or one of them- are absent, it will not happen. Al-Saadi: 485.\nWhen can one benefit from the means?\nقُلۡنَا يَٰذَا ٱلۡقَرۡنَيۡنِ إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمۡ حُسۡنٗا ٨٦\nMeaning: Allah gave him power over them, and gave him choice. If he wanted to, he could kill the men, and take the women and children captive, or if he wanted to, he could set them free, with or without a ransom. His justice and faith became apparent in the ruling he pronounced. Ibn Kathir: 3/100.\nThe believers are the most compassionate among people toward others. Explain in view of this verse.\nوَأَمَّا مَنۡ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا فَلَهُۥ جَزَآءً ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰۖ وَسَنَقُولُ لَهُۥ مِنۡ أَمۡرِنَا يُسۡرٗا ٨٨\nMeaning: Paradise will be his, and he will be in good standing before Allah, as a reward on the Day of Resurrection. (And we will enjoin upon him to do what is easy), we will treat him kindly, speak gently to him, and be easy going with him. This indicates that Thul-Qarnayn was a righteous, knowledgeable and a just king, as he dealt with each person according to his situation, which is in accordance with what is pleasing to Allah. Al-Saadi: 485.\nWhat is the sign of success for a righteous ruler?\nقَالُواْ يَٰذَا ٱلۡقَرۡنَيۡنِ إِنَّ يَأۡجُوجَ وَمَأۡجُوجَ مُفۡسِدُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَهَلۡ نَجۡعَلُ لَكَ خَرۡجًا عَلَىٰٓ أَن تَجۡعَلَ بَيۡنَنَا وَبَيۡنَهُمۡ سَدّٗا ٩٤ قَالَ مَا مَكَّنِّي فِيهِ رَبِّي خَيۡرٞ فَأَعِينُونِي بِقُوَّةٍ أَجۡعَلۡ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَبَيۡنَهُمۡ رَدۡمًا ٩٥\nThis verse proves that a ruler is obligated to protect his people, maintain their security, and fortify their borders using their public funds that they gain from outside sources, and what is available in their treasury. In case these public funds fall short, then they all have to compensate for it out of their own wealth. The ruler must manage these public funds wisely in accordance with these three conditions, first: He must not take exclusive possession of these funds. Second: He must start by helping the needy among them. Third: He must maintain equality among them in accordance with their eligibility. Al-Qurtubi: 13/384-385.\nExplain the duties of the Muslim ruler toward his people.\nقَالَ مَا مَكَّنِّي فِيهِ رَبِّي خَيۡرٞ فَأَعِينُونِي بِقُوَّةٍ أَجۡعَلۡ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَبَيۡنَهُمۡ رَدۡمًا ٩٥\nMeaning: Thul-Qarnayn told them: What Allah has given me of ability and sovereignty are much better than your reward and wealth. Al-Qurtubi: 13/384.\nDid Thul-Qarnayn become deluded by his sovereignty and ability, and forget Allah Who gave him all that?\nwords\nسَبَبًاThe means to achieve everything\nفَأَتبَعَ سَبَبًاSo he pursued a course\nحَمِئَةٍA hot spring of black muddy water\nنُكرًاA terrible punishment\nخَرجًاA financial reward\nرَدمًاA dam, barrier"],[304,"§Al-Kahf\ndeeds\nWhenever you complete an act of worship today, ask Allah to accept it from you.\nSeek refuge with Allah from shirk, innovation and show off.\nList the righteous deeds mentioned in Surat Al-Kahf and do one of them so you may attain the Gardens of Paradise.\nguid\nEvery time you help someone, thank Allah that He made it easy for you.\nA deed will have no value nor worth if it does not earn Allah's pleasure and acceptance.\ngood deed has to be done with sincerity and in accordance with the Sunnah of the Messenger (ﷺ) through authentic proof. Everything else is rejected even if it appears good.\nrefl\nوَعَرَضۡنَا جَهَنَّمَ يَوۡمَئِذٖ لِّلۡكَٰفِرِينَ عَرۡضًا ١٠٠\nAllah will show Hell to them, which means that He will bring it forth for them to see its punishment and torment before they enter it. This will intensify their distress and grief. Ibn Kathir: 3/104.\nWhy will Hellfire be shown to the disbelievers before they enter it on the Day of Resurrection?\nٱلَّذِينَ كَانَتۡ أَعۡيُنُهُمۡ فِي غِطَآءٍ عَن ذِكۡرِي وَكَانُواْ لَا يَسۡتَطِيعُونَ سَمۡعًا ١٠١\nMeaning: They could not bear to hear the verses of Allah which lead to faith because of their resentment toward the Quran and the Messenger (ﷺ), for the one who is filled with resentment cannot bear to hear the words of the one whom he resents. Once the ways of knowledge and goodness are blocked to them, they have no way to hear or see, and no reasoning that could benefit them. Al-Saadi: 487.\nThose who resent Islam cannot hear the verses of the Quran in a useful way. Why?\nأَفَحَسِبَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَن يَتَّخِذُواْ عِبَادِي مِن دُونِيٓ أَوۡلِيَآءَۚ إِنَّآ أَعۡتَدۡنَا جَهَنَّمَ لِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ نُزُلٗا ١٠٢\nCalling the torment of Hellfire a (lodging) is a metaphor intended for ridicule. Ibn Ashur: 16/45.\nWhy is the torment of Hellfire called a (lodging)?\nقُلۡ هَلۡ نُنَبِّئُكُم بِٱلۡأَخۡسَرِينَ أَعۡمَٰلًا ١٠٣ ٱلَّذِينَ ضَلَّ سَعۡيُهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَهُمۡ يَحۡسَبُونَ أَنَّهُمۡ يُحۡسِنُونَ صُنۡعًا ١٠٤\nThis proves that one may do deeds believing that he is a doer of good, but his deeds are nullified due to either his corrupt belief or showing off. Al-Qurtubi: 13/392.\nThe servant's deed may become nullified while he is unaware. Why?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّهِمۡ وَلِقَآئِهِۦ فَحَبِطَتۡ أَعۡمَٰلُهُمۡ فَلَا نُقِيمُ لَهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ وَزۡنٗا ١٠٥\nTheir nullified deeds will result in not giving weight to them because no good deeds left for them, thus, they will become disdained. Ibn Ashur: 16/48.\nThere will be no weight given to the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection. Why?\nلَا يَبۡغُونَ عَنۡهَا حِوَلٗا ١٠٨\nMeaning: They will never want to leave or move from there because they do not see anything but that which amazes and delights them, gives them joy and happiness, and they cannot imagine any bliss greater than that in which they are. Al-Saadi: 488.\nThe dwellers of Paradise will not want to move away from it to something else. Why?\nقُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أَنَا۠ بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيَّ أَنَّمَآ إِلَٰهُكُمۡ إِلَٰهٞ وَٰحِدٞۖ\nIbn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \"Allah taught humbleness to His Messenger (ﷺ), lest he would be boastful, and ordered him to say: I am a human just like you except I am given the revelation from Allah who honored me with it.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/70.\nExplain the importance of humbleness from this verse.\nwords\nدَكَّاءَLeveled to the ground\nفَحَبِطَتHave become worthless\nحِوَلًاA transfer\nلَنَفِدَFinished, depleted\nمَدَدًاInk"],[305,"§Maryam\ndeeds\nIdentify a difficult issue that you are facing, then call upon your Lord privately while having good expectations of Allah.\nAsk Allah to grant you righteous offspring and make them of His allies.\nRemember Allah often in the morning and evening.\nguid\nHave good expectations of Allah, for He is as His servant expects Him to be.\nReflecting on Allah's answer to the prayers of those who ask Him motivates you to invoke Him often.\nDo not measure your wishes against your capability, rather measure them against the power of Allah.\nrefl\nذِكۡرُ رَحۡمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبۡدَهُۥ زَكَرِيَّآ ٢\n[This is a mention of the mercy of your Lord to His slave Zachariah]. Allah describes His Prophet Zachariah as His (slave) to honor him, and signify his closeness to Him. Ibn Juzay: 2/3.\nAllah describes His Prophet Zachariah as His (slave), why?\nإِذۡ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُۥ نِدَآءً خَفِيّٗا ٣\n(When he called upon his Lord), he supplicated Him. (In private), he did it in secret because Allah hears what is hidden as well as the declared. Moreover, doing something in private is closer to sincerity and far from showing off, lest he would be blamed by others for asking Allah for a son. Ibn Juzay: 2/3.\nDescribing the call of Zachariah as (private) indicates several things. Explain.\nقَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَهَنَ ٱلۡعَظۡمُ مِنِّي وَٱشۡتَعَلَ ٱلرَّأۡسُ شَيۡبٗا\nHe prayed to Allah, expressing his weakness and incapability, and this is one of the dearest means of approaching Allah, because it is declaring one's lack of power and strength, and relying on the power and strength of Allah. Al-Saadi: 489.\nThe story of Zachariah reveals an effective means of asking Allah. What is it?\nقَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَهَنَ ٱلۡعَظۡمُ مِنِّي وَٱشۡتَعَلَ ٱلرَّأۡسُ شَيۡبٗا وَلَمۡ أَكُنۢ بِدُعَآئِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيّٗا ٤\nScholars said: It is recommended for one who supplicates Allah to mention His blessings upon him, and display submissiveness to Him as Zachariah said: (my bones have weakened). Moreover, saying: (Yet never have I been disappointed in my prayer to You, my Lord) is a mention of previous blessings from Allah by answering his supplication; meaning that whenever I supplicated You, You would always answer me. Al-Qurtubi: 13/409.\nWhat should be the demeanor of one who supplicates Allah humbly?\nوَإِنِّي خِفۡتُ ٱلۡمَوَٰلِيَ مِن وَرَآءِي وَكَانَتِ ٱمۡرَأَتِي عَاقِرٗا فَهَبۡ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ وَلِيّٗا ٥ يَرِثُنِي وَيَرِثُ مِنۡ ءَالِ يَعۡقُوبَۖ\nThe reason for his fear was that he was afraid that the generation that would succeed him would be a wicked generation to the people. Thus, he asked Allah for a son who would be a Prophet after him, who would guide them with his Prophethood and what was revealed to him, so his prayer was answered. It should be noted that he was not afraid of them inheriting his wealth, for a Prophet is too great in status, and too lofty in esteem to become remorseful over his wealth in this fashion. Ibn Kathir: 3/109.\nWas Zachariah afraid that his inheritors would inherit his wealth after death, similar to what is done by most people today? Were the Prophets actually been inherited by others?\nيَٰزَكَرِيَّآ إِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلَٰمٍ ٱسۡمُهُۥ يَحۡيَىٰ لَمۡ نَجۡعَل لَّهُۥ مِن قَبۡلُ سَمِيّٗا ٧\nThis glad tidings contained three things, first: Answering his supplication, which was an honor to him. Second: Granting him a son, which was adding strength to him. Third: The special name given to his son had not been given to anyone before. Al-Qurtubi: 13/417.\nThe glad tidings that Allah gave to His Prophet Zachariah (u) contained three things. What are they?\nقَالَ رَبِّ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي غُلَٰمٞ وَكَانَتِ ٱمۡرَأَتِي عَاقِرٗا وَقَدۡ بَلَغۡتُ مِنَ ٱلۡكِبَرِ عِتِيّٗا ٨\nZachariah was astonished, and he ruled out the possibility of begetting a son while he was extremely old and his wife was barren. Nevertheless, he asked Allah for that first because he knew His power, yet he became astonished since that was a rare incident. It is said that he asked Allah when he was younger, and he was answered after he became old. Ibn Juzay: 2/4.\nWhy did Zachariah become astonished when he received the glad tidings of a son even though he asked Allah for that?\nwords\nنَادَىHe called upon\nوَهَنَWeakened\nالمَوَالِيَKinsmen\nعَاقِرًاA barren woman\nعِتِيًّاAn extremely old age\nبُكرَةً وَعَشِيًّاMorning and afternoon"],[306,"§Maryam\ndeeds\nDo your utmost to adhere to your religion, and beware of mucking about in adherence to its rules.\nWhen Mary saw Gabriel, she was terrified and sought help from Allah, not anyone else.\nAdopt the means to reach an end, and do not fall behind while depending on others.\nguid\nGive your parents something that they like.\nSeek refuge with Allah, today, from any one whom you fear his evil deed.\nEat seven dates first thing in the morning.\nrefl\nوَبَرَّۢا بِوَٰلِدَيۡهِ وَلَمۡ يَكُن جَبَّارًا عَصِيّٗا ١٤\n(And dutiful to his parents), he hastened to their obedience and love, and never was ungrateful to them. (And he was not a disobedient tyrant), he was not arrogant, nor did he resent obeying Allah and his parents. Moreover, he was humble to Allah and his parents, and acting upon what he was enjoined and refraining from what was forbidden. He never disobeys His Lord or his parents. Al-Tabari: 18/160.\nThis verse contains two rights. What are they?\nوَسَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡهِ يَوۡمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوۡمَ يَمُوتُ وَيَوۡمَ يُبۡعَثُ حَيّٗا ١٥\nSufyan bin Uyaynah said: \"The loneliest that a man will ever feel is in three situations. First: On the day he is born, he sees himself coming out of what he was in [safe place]. Second: On the day that he dies, he sees beings whom he had never seen before. Third: On the day when he is resurrected, he sees himself in the great gathering. Allah has exclusively honored John, the son of Zachariah, by granting him peace in these situations.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/111.\nPeace upon John (u) is mentioned in these three situations only. Why?\nقَالَتۡ إِنِّيٓ أَعُوذُ بِٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ مِنكَ إِن كُنتَ تَقِيّٗا ١٨\nReminding him of Allah; this is what is ordained in pushing against evil. It is warded off by using the easier way first, thus, the first thing she did was trying to make him fear Allah, the Mighty and Sublime. Ibn Kathir: 3/113.\nWhat is the ideal approach for fending off aggression against oneself?\nقَالَتۡ إِنِّيٓ أَعُوذُ بِٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ مِنكَ إِن كُنتَ تَقِيّٗا ١٨\nMary (o) mentioned Allah's attribute (the Most Merciful), because she wanted Allah to be merciful to her by warding off what she thought was an evil person. Ibn Ashur: 16/81.\nMary singled out Allah's attribute (the Most Merciful) for mention. Why?\nوَلِنَجۡعَلَهُۥٓ ءَايَةٗ لِّلنَّاسِ\nThat will point to the perfect might of Allah, and highlight the fact that no cause can lead to its effect independently of Allah, rather, the effect comes about by the decree of Allah. Hence, Allah shows His servants extraordinary events concerning some ordinary causes or means, lest they become attached to these means, and ignore the One Who controls and decrees them. Al-Saadi: 491.\nThe story of Mary and her son makes people's hearts become attached only to Allah with disregard to worldly means. Explain.\nوَهُزِّيٓ إِلَيۡكِ بِجِذۡعِ ٱلنَّخۡلَةِ تُسَٰقِطۡ عَلَيۡكِ رُطَبٗا جَنِيّٗا ٢٥\nThis verse is quoted as evidence by some people that one should strive for his provision since Allah has commanded Mary to shake the trunk of the palm tree. Ibn Juzay: 2/6.\nIt is inferred from this verse that one should strive for his provision. Explain\nوَهُزِّيٓ إِلَيۡكِ بِجِذۡعِ ٱلنَّخۡلَةِ تُسَٰقِطۡ عَلَيۡكِ رُطَبٗا جَنِيّٗا ٢٥ فَكُلِي وَٱشۡرَبِي وَقَرِّي عَيۡنٗاۖ\nSome scholars inferred from this verse that the best food for a postnatal woman is ripe dates. Al-Rabi bin Khuthaym and others said: \"If there was better a food suited for a postnatal woman than ripe dates, Allah would have fed Mary after delivering Jesus (u).\" Al-Shanqiti: 3/399.\nThis verse presents good medical approach. What is it?\nwords\nخُذِ الكِتَابThe Torah\nبِقُوَّةٍWith strength, determination\nالحُكمَThe wisdom\nوَحَنَانًاAffection and love\nانتَبَذَتShe withdrew in seclusion\nفَأَجَاءَهَاDrove her\nالمَخَاضُThe pains of childbirth\nسَرِيًّاA water stream\nجَنِيًّاFresh"],[307,"§Maryam\ndeeds\nDefend an oppressed person today with the best means you can.\nPerform the daily prayers in congregation, then pray the regular Sunnah prayers.\nRead the story of Jesus (u) from a reliable source.\nguid\nDo not hasten to judge righteous people, as there may be things of which you are unaware.\nUphold prayer and zakah as long as you live, for that is the mark of Prophets and righteous people.\nDutifulness to parents is the attribute of Prophets and righteous people.\nrefl\nفَلَنۡ أُكَلِّمَ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ إِنسِيّٗا ٢٦\nShe was instructed not to speak to them, and say that she had done nothing wrong or defend herself, because the people would not believe her, and there was no benefit in doing that. The declaration of her innocence coming from the words of Jesus (u) when he spoke in the cradle would be a more effective testimony of her innocence. For a woman to have a child without a husband, and claim that he had no father would be a most serious claim, and even if there were many witnesses, it would not be believed. Therefore, the proof of this extraordinary event was made to be of the same nature as the event itself, which was the speaking of Jesus (u) in his infancy. Al-Saadi: 492.\nWhy was Mary (o) instructed not to speak to anyone about Jesus (u)?\nفَأَتَتۡ بِهِۦ قَوۡمَهَا تَحۡمِلُهُ\nShe brought Jesus (u) to her people, carrying him in her arms, because she knew of her innocence and purity. Al-Saadi: 492.\nHow did Mary (o) gather the courage to meet her people carrying Jesus (u) despite being a single woman?\nقَالَ إِنِّي عَبۡدُ ٱللَّهِ ءَاتَىٰنِيَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَجَعَلَنِي نَبِيّٗا ٣٠\nIn this verse, Allah mentions that the first words uttered by Jesus (u) while he was a child in the cradle were: He is a slave of Allah; and this is a sharp rebuke to the Christians for their claim that he is god, a son of God, or a partner with God. Al-Shanqiti: 3/416.\nWhat can be understood from the first words uttered by Jesus (u)?\nقَالَ إِنِّي عَبۡدُ ٱللَّهِ\nHe addressed them, referring to himself as a slave of Allah, and stating that he possessed no attributes for which he might deserve to be taken as a god or as the son of God; exalted be Allah far above what the Christians, who claim to be followers of Jesus (u) but drifted away from his path, say concerning him, which is contrary to what Jesus (u) himself said. Al-Saadi: 492.\nThe first words uttered by Jesus (u) were, (Indeed, I am the slave of Allah). Why?\nوَجَعَلَنِي مُبَارَكًا أَيۡنَ مَا كُنتُ\n(Blessed), beneficial wherever I go. Mujahid said: \"A teacher of good.\" Ata' said: \"I invite others to the Oneness of Allah and to worship Him.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/85.\nHow can a servant be blessed, wherever he may be?\nوَبَرَّۢا بِوَٰلِدَتِي وَلَمۡ يَجۡعَلۡنِي جَبَّارٗا شَقِيّٗا ٣٢\nAllah selected him to be dutiful to his mother from among his people, because dutifulness to parents was weak in the community of Children of Israel; especially the mother due to her weakness and compassion, which may call her son to neglect being dutiful to her. Ibn Ashur: 16/100.\nAllah mentions Jesus' (u) dutifulness to his mother. Why?\nوَٱلسَّلَٰمُ عَلَيَّ يَوۡمَ وُلِدتُّ وَيَوۡمَ أَمُوتُ وَيَوۡمَ أُبۡعَثُ حَيّٗا ٣٣\nJesus (u) mentioned these situations in which man needs the mercy of Allah. Ibn Atiyah: 4/15.\nPeace upon Jesus (u) is mentioned by him for these three situations only. Why?\nwords\nوَقَرِّي عَينًاAnd be contented\nفَرِيًّا أَمرًاA thing unprecedented\nبَغِيًّاUnchaste woman\nمُبَارَكًاBlessed\nيَمتَرُونَThey are in doubt\nالأَحزَابُThe factions among the people of the Book\nفَوَيلٌWoe, punishment\nمَشهَدِWitnessing\nأَسمِع بِهِم وَأَبصِرHow clearly they will hear and see"],[308,"§Maryam\ndeeds\nPursue the divine reward when you are affected by a trial. Abraham (u) was trialed by the disbelief of his father, but he was patient with Allah's decree; therefore, Allah placed Prophethood in his descendants.\nThe story of Abraham (u) and his father is full of useful lessons; try to summarize them in several points, and share them with those around you.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness and mercy for your parents.\nguid\nWorshiping idols, gravesites or shrines is considered worshiping the devil, because he orders it and calls others to do it.\nDo not be too proud to seek knowledge from one who is younger or at a lower social rank than you.\nDistance yourself from places of evil and corruption, and do not be tolerant of that.\nrefl\nوَأَنذِرۡهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡحَسۡرَةِ إِذۡ قُضِيَ ٱلۡأَمۡرُ وَهُمۡ فِي غَفۡلَةٖ وَهُمۡ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٣٩\nIn the Arabic text, the word used is \"hasrah\", which indicates the most severe regret to the point of harming one's life over what is missed and cannot be recovered. Warning is: Informing and threatening, which means: Warn the people of the Day of Resurrection. It is called the Day of Regret, because the disbelievers will become very remorseful for their negligence. The believers will also regret their shortcomings. Al-Shanqiti: 3/422.\nWhy was the Day of Resurrection called the \"Day of Regret\"? Will the regret be exclusive to the disbelievers?\nوَٱذۡكُرۡ فِي ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ صِدِّيقٗا نَّبِيًّا ٤١\nIn the original Arabic text, the word \"siddiq\", translated here as the man of truth. It is one who constantly speaks the truth and adheres to it. Moreover, it is said that whoever truly believes in the Oneness of Allah, in His Prophets and Messengers, in the Resurrection, and upholds His commands, is a \"siddiq.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/88.\nHow can a servant become \"siddiq\"?\nيَٰٓأَبَتِ لِمَ تَعۡبُدُ مَا لَا يَسۡمَعُ وَلَا يُبۡصِرُ وَلَا يُغۡنِي عَنكَ شَيۡـٔٗا ٤٢ يَٰٓأَبَتِ إِنِّي قَدۡ جَآءَنِي مِنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ مَا لَمۡ يَأۡتِكَ فَٱتَّبِعۡنِيٓ أَهۡدِكَ صِرَٰطٗا سَوِيّٗا ٤٣ يَٰٓأَبَتِ لَا تَعۡبُدِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَۖ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ كَانَ لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِ عَصِيّٗا ٤٤ يَٰٓأَبَتِ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ أَن يَمَسَّكَ عَذَابٞ مِّنَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ فَتَكُونَ لِلشَّيۡطَٰنِ وَلِيّٗا ٤٥\nAbraham (u) adopted a gradual approach in calling his father, starting with the easiest thing to accept, then, the next easiest. He informed him of his knowledge, and told him that this required him to follow him, for if he did, he would be guided to the straight path. Then, he told him not to worship satan, and informed him of the harmful outcome of doing so. Then he warned him of the punishment of Allah, if he carried on as he was, and told him that he would be a companion of satan. Al-Saadi: 495.\nThe gradual approach is an important method for the preacher to follow. How do we benefit from the approach in the story of Abraham (u) when calling others to Allah?\nيَٰٓأَبَتِ إِنِّي قَدۡ جَآءَنِي مِنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ مَا لَمۡ يَأۡتِكَ\nThis is obviously a gentle approach in speech, as he avoided saying, \"O my father, I know, and you do not know\" or \"You do not know anything.\" Rather, he said it in a way that implied we both have knowledge, but what has reached me has not reached you. Al-Saadi: 494.\nHow does a preacher benefit from this verse when calling others to Allah?\nيَٰٓأَبَتِ لَا تَعۡبُدِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَۖ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَ كَانَ لِلرَّحۡمَٰنِ عَصِيّٗا ٤٤\nIn the Arabic text, the word used is (asia'a) in a context which indicates that the devil is extremely rebellious against his Lord in a continuous pace. Ibn Ashur: 16/117.\nWhy is the devil described as (asia'a)?\nقَالَ سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡكَۖ سَأَسۡتَغۡفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّيٓۖ\nAbraham (u) responded to him in the manner of the servants of the Most Gracious when addressing the ignorant. He did not revile him, rather, he was patient, and he did not respond to him in an offensive manner. He said: (Peace will be upon you). Al-Saadi: 495.\nHow should the preacher behave when faced with abuse and offensive words?\nوَأَعۡتَزِلُكُمۡ وَمَا تَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَأَدۡعُواْ رَبِّي عَسَىٰٓ أَلَّآ أَكُونَ بِدُعَآءِ رَبِّي شَقِيّٗا ٤٨\nThis is what a person should do when he despairs of those whom he is calling to Islam; he should focus on purifying his own soul and hope for acceptance from his Lord, and he should keep away from evil and its people. Al-Saadi: 495.\nWhat should the preacher do when he does not find acceptance from those whom he calls to Allah?\nwords\nالحَسرَةِRegret\nصِدِّيقًاA man of truth\nصِرَاطًا سَوِيًّاA straight path\nمَلِيًّاA long time\nحَفِيًّاHe is ever gracious to me\nمُخلَصًاHe was chosen"],[309,"§Maryam\ndeeds\nEnjoin your brothers and family members prayer and zakah, and remind them to perform them during their prescribed times.\nWhen reciting the Quran, weep or try to, especially when you are alone.\nRecall a sin that you had committed, then ask for Allah's forgiveness persistently, and repent from it.\nguid\nBe truthful in your words, deeds, promises and covenants, for that is among the traits of the Prophets.\nChecking on family members and relatives for performing prayer and zakah is among the traits of the Prophets.\nPay attention to your prayer every so often, because neglecting prayer is a neglection of religion.\nrefl\nوَٱذۡكُرۡ فِي ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ إِسۡمَٰعِيلَۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ صَادِقَ ٱلۡوَعۡدِ وَكَانَ رَسُولٗا نَّبِيّٗا ٥٤\nMujahid said: \"He kept every promise he made.\" Muqatil said: \"He promised to wait in a place for a man, and Ishmael stayed in the same place for three days until the man came back to him.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/91.\nExplain the importance of keeping the promise to the Prophets (p).\nوَٱذۡكُرۡ فِي ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ إِسۡمَٰعِيلَۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ صَادِقَ ٱلۡوَعۡدِ وَكَانَ رَسُولٗا نَّبِيّٗا ٥٤ وَكَانَ يَأۡمُرُ أَهۡلَهُۥ بِٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَٱلزَّكَوٰةِ\nIshmael strove to perfect himself, and to perfect others, especially the dearest of people to him, namely his family, because they were more deserving of his call than others. Al-Saadi: 496.\nWhy were his people singled out for mention in this verse?\nإِذَا تُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ خَرُّواْۤ سُجَّدٗاۤ وَبُكِيّٗا۩ ٥٨\nAttributing the revelations to the divine name (the Most Merciful) indicates that the revelations are part of His mercy and kindness toward His servants, as He guided them thereby to the truth, made their blind eyes see, saved them from misguidance, and granted them knowledge when they were ignorant. Al-Saadi: 496.\nWhat is the benefit of attributing the revelations to the divine name (the Most Merciful)?\nفَخَلَفَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ خَلۡفٌ أَضَاعُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَٱتَّبَعُواْ ٱلشَّهَوَٰتِۖ فَسَوۡفَ يَلۡقَوۡنَ غَيًّا ٥٩\nIbn Masoud (t) was asked about the meaning of neglecting prayer, and he said: \"It is the delay in performing prayer until its time has passed.\" They said, \"We considered that abandonment of prayer.\" He replied, \"If they abandoned prayer, then they would become disbelievers.\" Ibn Taimyah: 4/285.\nExplain the risk of delaying prayer beyond its prescribed time.\nفَخَلَفَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ خَلۡفٌ أَضَاعُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ\nIf they neglected prayer, then they would be prone to neglect other obligatory acts of worship, because prayer is the pillar and foundation of Islam, and it is the best of the servants' deeds. Ibn Kathir: 3/125.\nSingling out prayer for mention is an indication of something important. What is it?\nجَنَّٰتِ عَدۡنٍ ٱلَّتِي وَعَدَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ عِبَادَهُۥ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِۚ\nAllah refers to Himself as (the Most Merciful), because of what this reward contains of mercy and generosity, such as no eye has seen, no ear has heard, nor has it ever crossed the mind of man. Moreover, attributing it to His mercy is indicative of the abiding nature of its bliss, for it will remain, as long as, His mercy remains, of which it (Paradise) is the outcome and result. Al-Saadi: 497.\nWhat is the benefit of linking the mention of Gardens of Eternity to the divine name (the Most Merciful) in this verse?\nوَلَهُمۡ رِزۡقُهُمۡ فِيهَا بُكۡرَةٗ وَعَشِيّٗا ٦٢\n(Morning and afternoon), similar to the interval of these two time periods, because there will be no morning or afternoon. Scholars said: In Paradise, there is no night or day because there will be only light. Al-Qurtubi: 13/479.\nHow will the people of Paradise have their provision, morning and afternoon? Will Paradise have day and night?\nwords\nالطُّورMount Sinai\nنَجِيًّاCommuning with Allah\nوَإِسرَائِيلَProphet Jacob (u)\nوَاجتَبَينَاWe chose\nخَلفٌEvil successors\nغَيًّاEvil in Hellfire\nمَأتِيًّاWill surely be fulfilled\nلَغوًاIdle talk"],[310,"§Maryam\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the torment of Hell, for it is assured that you will come to it, but there is no assurance of being saved from it.\nAsk Allah to make you among those whom He increases in guidance.\nSay, \"Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is none worthy of worship but Allah, Allah is the greatest,\" as these words are the righteous deeds of lasting merit.\nguid\nWorship requires patience and effort, so become used to that.\nA befitting recompense; the leaders in disbelief and misguidance will be dragged out to Hellfire before their followers.\nWhoever pursues good knowledge or righteous deed while he is adamant and sincere, Allah will guide him to more good knowledge and righteous deeds.\nrefl\nفَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَحۡشُرَنَّهُمۡ وَٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ ثُمَّ لَنُحۡضِرَنَّهُمۡ حَوۡلَ جَهَنَّمَ جِثِيّٗا ٦٨\nAdding (the devils) to the polytheists is meant to disdain them in that they will be gathered with the worst and most corrupt beings. It also indicates that the devils are the cause of their misguidance which brought them to this situation. Ibn Ashur: 16/147.\nWhat is the wisdom behind adding the devils to the polytheists?\nثُمَّ لَنَنزِعَنَّ مِن كُلِّ شِيعَةٍ أَيُّهُمۡ أَشَدُّ عَلَى ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ عِتِيّٗا ٦٩\n(Those who were most rebellious against the Most Merciful), most obstinate. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \"It means the most defiant.\" Mujahid said: \"The most wicked,\" which means the most rebellious first then the lesser one next. Al-Kalbi said: \"Their leader and head of evil,\" which means the first one to be dragged out to Hell will be the worst criminal and the biggest in disbelief. Some say that they will all be gathered around Hell in chains, then the biggest in disbelief will be dragged out to Hell first. Al-Baghawi: 3/99.\nExplain the punishment of the one who is a leader in evil and tyranny.\nوَإِن مِّنكُمۡ إِلَّا وَارِدُهَاۚ كَانَ عَلَىٰ رَبِّكَ حَتۡمٗا مَّقۡضِيّٗا ٧١\nAbdullah bin Rawahah (t) wept while leaning his head on his wife's lap, who also wept with him, and he said: \"Why are you weeping?\" She replied, \"I wept when I saw you weeping.\" He said: \"I recalled Allah's saying: (And there is none among you except that he will pass over it), and I do not know if I will be saved from it or not!\" When Abu Maysarah goes to bed, he used to say, \"I wish I had not been born!\" hen he began weeping, and so it was said to him, \"What is the matter, Abu Maysarah?\" He said, \"We were told that we will come to it [Hellfire], but we were not told that we will be saved from it.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/129.\nThose who reflect on the meanings of the Quran are fearful of coming to Hellfire. Why?\nوَإِذَا تُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتُنَا بَيِّنَٰتٖ قَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَيُّ ٱلۡفَرِيقَيۡنِ خَيۡرٞ مَّقَامٗا وَأَحۡسَنُ نَدِيّٗا ٧٣\n(Which of the two groups, us or the believers, is better in terms of dwellings), in this world, and in terms of large amounts of wealth, large numbers of children and fulfilment of desires. Thus it is known that concluding that one will be in a good situation in the Hereafter, because he is in a good situation in this world is one of the most flawed arguments, and is the way of thinking of the disbelievers. Al-Saadi: 499.\nPeople often believe that having worldly blessings is a sign of Allah's love for them. What do you think?\nوَكَمۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَا قَبۡلَهُم مِّن قَرۡنٍ هُمۡ أَحۡسَنُ أَثَٰثٗا وَرِءۡيٗا ٧٤\n(Possessions): Wealth and clothing, etc. (Appearance): Exterior image. Allah states that those whom He destroyed before them used to have better images, clothing and wealth in order to show that all of these things neither benefit them with Allah, nor does He care about them. Ibn Taimyah: 4/292.\nWealth and images do not benefit their owners with Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُلۡ مَن كَانَ فِي ٱلضَّلَٰلَةِ فَلۡيَمۡدُدۡ لَهُ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ مَدًّاۚ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا رَأَوۡاْ مَا يُوعَدُونَ إِمَّا ٱلۡعَذَابَ وَإِمَّا ٱلسَّاعَةَ فَسَيَعۡلَمُونَ مَنۡ هُوَ شَرّٞ مَّكَانٗا وَأَضۡعَفُ جُندٗا ٧٥\nThe criterion for differentiating between one who has a blessing due to Allah's pleasure with him, and another who has a blessing that gradually leads him to his doom - is to look whether his way of life adheres to guidance or misguidance. Ibn Ashur: 16/155.\nHow do we distinguish between one who has a blessing due to Allah's pleasure with him and another who has a blessing that gradually leads him to his doom?\nوَٱلۡبَٰقِيَٰتُ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ خَيۡرٌ عِندَ رَبِّكَ ثَوَابٗا وَخَيۡرٞ مَّرَدًّا ٧٦\n(And the righteous deeds of lasting merit): Athkar (remembrance of Allah) and righteous deeds which last for its doer. Al-Baghawi: 3/105.\nWhat are the righteous deeds of lasting merit? Why is it called as such?\nwords\nجِثِيًّاOn their knees\nعِتِيًّاMost rebellious\nصِلِيًّاMost deserving to burn\nوَارِدُهَاPassing over the bridge on top of Hellfire\nنَدِيًّاSocial gatherings\nأَثَاثًاPossessions\nوَرِئيًاOutward appearance\nمَرَدًّاRecourse, outcome"]])